{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel.</b> This sign was greater than all the signs performed through Moses, for there were many signs in the manna, and they lasted forty years, unlike all the other signs." "And the meaning of \"unto a settled land\": for they were in the wilderness, in a land through which no man passed (Jeremiah 2:6). And behold, when they crossed the Jordan they ate the produce they found, therefore it was necessary to say, \"they ate the manna until they came to the border of the land of Canaan,\" for the manna continued with them until they came to Gilgal, which is the border of the land of Canaan. And behold, new produce was available to them; then the manna ceased."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:15.283308525Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}